WEBVTT

01:42.018 --> 01:46.940
THE GRAVITY OF BEING A LAND DWELLER

01:48.316 --> 01:50.443
Don't touch him!

01:53.154 --> 01:54.280
You bastard!

01:59.327 --> 02:03.039
I guess I should finish
my lecture, Legoshi.

02:03.623 --> 02:07.460
There's more to that policy
I was bugging you about.

02:08.211 --> 02:11.506
Pacifism is commendable, indeed.

02:11.589 --> 02:17.220
But it's only meaningful
when proclaimed by those with strength.

02:37.198 --> 02:39.993
Shall we finish him off, Legoshi?

02:40.076 --> 02:41.244
Finish?

02:51.629 --> 02:54.048
Birds are lightweight so they can fly.

02:54.132 --> 02:56.593
They're no good at fighting on land.

02:56.676 --> 03:00.263
You know your stuff.
So you've been in your share of fights?

03:00.346 --> 03:02.849
No! I've just read about it
in a book somewhere.

03:05.435 --> 03:10.398
Well, these punks just got roughed up
a little by this old geezer.

03:12.400 --> 03:14.569
They'll come to their senses before long.

03:17.906 --> 03:19.240
Legoshi.

03:19.324 --> 03:22.285
I was worried about you,

03:23.077 --> 03:27.123
but it looks like
you won't need my help anymore.

03:36.382 --> 03:39.093
It looks like you're
enjoying that wine, Azuki.

03:39.969 --> 03:45.225
Almost as much as you enjoyed
your asparagus tagliolini.

03:45.308 --> 03:50.813
The buttercream sauce
with asparagus was truly elegant.

03:51.397 --> 03:53.524
I'm glad you have an appetite.

03:54.984 --> 04:00.114
My father told me you lost your right leg.

04:00.198 --> 04:02.867
That's right. I was in an accident.

04:03.409 --> 04:06.204
It was a miracle my life was saved.

04:06.704 --> 04:07.830
I see.

04:09.082 --> 04:11.417
So it hasn't affected
your reproductive abilities?

04:12.543 --> 04:13.544
Excuse me?

04:13.628 --> 04:16.214
It's important, you know.

04:16.297 --> 04:20.468
We wouldn't want to find out
after marriage that we can't have kids.

04:22.095 --> 04:27.976
The Horns Conglomerate isn't so desperate
as to entertain such a rude question here.

04:29.435 --> 04:31.771
That's surprisingly naive of you to say.

04:34.274 --> 04:39.404
I should have known better
and invited you in a more charming way.

04:41.197 --> 04:42.615
I've got a room here.

04:44.409 --> 04:49.122
We'll be married soon.
Why don't we try getting a bit closer?

04:59.465 --> 05:00.633
Azuki!

05:00.717 --> 05:03.803
What is it? You don't like this?

05:03.886 --> 05:05.972
No, it's just...

05:06.055 --> 05:07.557
I'm thirsty.

05:10.435 --> 05:14.063
<i>God, I'm such a virgin. Pathetic.</i>

05:15.023 --> 05:19.569
<i>The very idea of carnivores
and herbivores coexisting in society</i>

05:19.652 --> 05:21.571
<i>is contrary to the laws of nature!</i>

05:21.654 --> 05:23.573
<i>Isn't that a bit extreme?</i>

05:24.157 --> 05:29.078
<i>Without mutual cooperation,
society as we know it wouldn't even exist.</i>

05:29.162 --> 05:32.081
<i>If we'd been kept separate from the start...</i>

05:32.206 --> 05:34.083
<i>Is this really okay?</i>

05:34.876 --> 05:37.003
<i>This kind of political arranged marriage.</i>

05:37.920 --> 05:40.465
<i>Is this really the right path for me?</i>

05:41.758 --> 05:44.469
<i>Louis, you saved me.</i>

05:53.519 --> 05:55.438
<i>Yes. This is what I want.</i>

05:57.065 --> 05:59.984
<i>Two fragile bodies becoming one.</i>

06:00.068 --> 06:02.737
<i>This is normal.
There's nothing strange about it.</i>

06:03.362 --> 06:05.740
<i>I'm the one who's strange.</i>

06:06.240 --> 06:08.868
<i>I don't know why I find this abnormal.</i>

06:13.039 --> 06:15.166
<i>This is different from Juno's kiss.</i>

06:15.917 --> 06:19.921
<i>I can't feel... those hard fangs.</i>

06:22.131 --> 06:24.592
<i>Don't compare them! Concentrate!</i>

06:24.675 --> 06:27.762
<i>Quit thinking strange thoughts
and getting off track!</i>

06:28.429 --> 06:29.263
<i>Do it!</i>

06:29.347 --> 06:31.265
<i>Do it. Do it. Do it!</i>

06:31.349 --> 06:32.642
<i>Azuki, my fellow deer,</i>

06:32.725 --> 06:34.519
<i>I'm going to make love to you!</i>

06:34.602 --> 06:36.687
<i>It's dangerous and abnormal!</i>

06:38.147 --> 06:40.441
Are you okay, Louis?

06:49.909 --> 06:51.369
<i>It seems...</i>

06:51.911 --> 06:54.372
<i>there really is something wrong with me.</i>

06:58.376 --> 07:00.294
FESTIVAL OF THE METEOR
JULY 27, FRIDAY

07:02.380 --> 07:04.590
This one isn't bad, either.

07:05.383 --> 07:08.386
MAYOR

07:25.903 --> 07:28.406
Hey! I told you not to call me.

07:29.115 --> 07:31.367
<i>Did you forget our deal?</i>

07:31.451 --> 07:36.664
<i>Why is that damn horse
still snooping around town?</i>

07:37.206 --> 07:38.749
Calm down.

07:39.250 --> 07:42.962
You reptiles just sit back
and bask in the sun.

07:43.880 --> 07:45.298
I'm on top of it.

08:00.021 --> 08:01.022
Are you okay?

08:02.648 --> 08:04.484
Who the hell were those guys?

08:04.567 --> 08:05.860
Screw this.

08:06.569 --> 08:08.237
Give me one of those.

08:15.620 --> 08:19.582
Hey, give me some too.
It's your fault this happened.

08:20.416 --> 08:21.417
Come on.

08:22.960 --> 08:26.547
- You don't have to get so angry.
- Calm down!

08:48.611 --> 08:50.154
How pathetic.

08:50.738 --> 08:53.991
You got beat up that bad
by one guy hopped up on Kines?

08:54.075 --> 08:57.745
It wasn't that. Some old guy got us.

08:57.828 --> 08:58.829
Old guy?

08:58.913 --> 09:00.957
A crazy old lizard.

09:01.040 --> 09:03.125
Damn that creepy venom user...

09:03.209 --> 09:04.710
<i>Venom user?</i>

09:05.545 --> 09:08.297
<i>Could it really be you?</i>

09:09.674 --> 09:13.010
<i>Why would you come out of the shadows now?</i>

09:13.636 --> 09:14.762
<i>You traitor.</i>

09:14.845 --> 09:17.723
<i>You turned your back on me
and abandoned this world.</i>

09:17.807 --> 09:22.103
36 YEARS EARLIER

09:22.728 --> 09:24.021
Wait up!

09:24.939 --> 09:26.649
Just take it.

09:29.026 --> 09:30.736
Careful!

09:31.320 --> 09:35.074
What a joke.
Why did they only give it to me?

09:35.157 --> 09:37.827
It was you who discovered the fire.

09:38.411 --> 09:41.455
I couldn't have saved the child on my own!

09:41.539 --> 09:43.165
It's not fair!

09:43.249 --> 09:45.876
Don't be angry. It's normal.

09:46.836 --> 09:49.171
Then "normal" can go to hell!

09:52.008 --> 09:54.343
I should have done that
in the first place.

09:54.885 --> 09:58.556
We deserve better than cheap medals.

10:01.142 --> 10:03.603
<i>I trusted you back then.</i>

10:04.770 --> 10:07.523
<i>The remaining 10 degrees of my vision.</i>

10:07.607 --> 10:08.858
<i>My partner.</i>

10:09.817 --> 10:14.280
<i>With you around, I never had to look back.</i>

10:15.698 --> 10:17.074
Hey, Gosha.

10:17.158 --> 10:19.285
Let's change the world.

10:19.368 --> 10:20.578
You and me.

10:22.038 --> 10:24.832
<i>We could accomplish anything together.</i>

10:26.292 --> 10:29.837
<i>Back then, neither Gosha nor I</i>

10:30.421 --> 10:32.340
<i>wanted to become a Beastar.</i>

10:32.423 --> 10:33.924
<i>We wanted to be two Beastars.</i>

10:36.010 --> 10:39.847
<i>But that night,
everything started to change.</i>

10:45.895 --> 10:49.315
What fine fur you have.
You'll make me some money.

10:49.815 --> 10:52.234
How about I start with your fangs?

10:53.277 --> 10:56.947
I'll be all done by the time you wake up.

11:09.960 --> 11:11.879
We made it just in time.

11:20.930 --> 11:22.223
Your scales...

11:22.306 --> 11:24.308
They're like jewels.

11:24.392 --> 11:25.643
So beautiful.

11:40.533 --> 11:42.618
Thank you.

11:44.120 --> 11:47.123
These incidents where beasts are drugged

11:47.206 --> 11:49.834
and skinned while they're asleep
have been on the rise.

11:50.584 --> 11:52.128
Be careful out there.

11:52.670 --> 11:55.756
Oh, I see.

11:55.840 --> 11:59.593
So I was about to become a fur coat?

12:02.513 --> 12:06.934
<i>By the next day,
Gosha and that girl were dating.</i>

12:07.643 --> 12:08.561
<i>And surprisingly...</i>

12:08.644 --> 12:09.770
SIX MONTHS LATER

12:09.854 --> 12:11.188
<i>...they were making it work.</i>

12:12.106 --> 12:14.066
A lizard and a wolf.

12:14.150 --> 12:16.944
That's a pretty crazy
interspecies pairing, isn't it?

12:18.279 --> 12:19.947
Do you really see eye to eye?

12:20.614 --> 12:22.283
If we didn't,

12:22.366 --> 12:24.368
we wouldn't have lasted this long.

12:26.328 --> 12:27.997
So, what did you want to tell me?

12:28.581 --> 12:30.207
Right...

12:31.333 --> 12:33.210
She's pregnant.

12:34.170 --> 12:35.421
With my child.

12:35.504 --> 12:38.507
What? Whose kid?

12:39.008 --> 12:41.093
I told you. It's mine.

12:41.177 --> 12:44.889
A mammal and a reptile?

12:44.972 --> 12:46.765
That shouldn't be possible!

12:47.391 --> 12:49.935
The doctor said it was a miracle.

12:50.436 --> 12:51.937
I've got to support them.

12:53.272 --> 12:55.024
Are you serious?

12:55.107 --> 12:57.443
Childbirth is going to be risky!

12:59.111 --> 13:00.154
Listen.

13:00.237 --> 13:03.782
This is not the time for you
to be starting a family!

13:04.533 --> 13:08.829
You and I are going to become Beastars
and change the world!

13:12.124 --> 13:13.250
I'm out.

13:19.590 --> 13:23.677
I wanted us to become Beastars
for the sake of peace and coexistence.

13:24.553 --> 13:30.392
But I found something even more important
than protecting society at large.

13:32.144 --> 13:35.189
So you're going to abandon me?

13:38.317 --> 13:39.443
<i>Traitor.</i>

13:52.623 --> 13:55.834
<i>I have a report about the wolf.</i>

13:55.918 --> 13:56.961
What did you find?

13:57.920 --> 14:00.172
<i>It appears he doesn't have parents,</i>

14:00.256 --> 14:03.676
<i>but his school documents
list his grandfather as his guardian.</i>

14:04.468 --> 14:08.472
<i>It's hard to believe,
but he's a Komodo dragon.</i>

14:10.724 --> 14:12.935
<i>Those eyes, those slanted eyebrows.</i>

14:14.687 --> 14:16.313
<i>I see the resemblance.</i>

14:17.273 --> 14:20.025
Invite him to the Carrot Party.

14:20.109 --> 14:21.277
<i>I'll make the arrangements.</i>

14:22.486 --> 14:25.823
UDON BEBEBE
OPEN

14:25.906 --> 14:31.036
<i>"I've got a problem.
Can you help me out? Bill."</i>

14:32.204 --> 14:33.539
I wonder what happened?

14:33.622 --> 14:35.124
Legoshi.

14:36.166 --> 14:37.209
Yes?

14:37.293 --> 14:41.297
I'm thinking about having you
start doing marine deliveries soon.

14:41.380 --> 14:43.090
Marine deliveries?

14:43.632 --> 14:46.552
Deliveries to our sea creature customers.

14:47.386 --> 14:51.181
Oh, of course... We deliver to them?

14:51.265 --> 14:55.144
Our restaurant is welcome to all species.
That's our motto.

14:55.227 --> 14:57.771
Just tell them you're from Udon Bebebe.

14:57.855 --> 15:02.276
But I don't speak
a lick of marine language.

15:02.359 --> 15:06.655
Legoshi, I thought you went to that
Cherryton School?

15:10.993 --> 15:12.119
Just say that.

15:13.120 --> 15:14.788
What? Can you repeat that for me?

15:14.872 --> 15:16.916
<i>A</i>... <i>abu</i>...

15:16.999 --> 15:18.000
Please!

15:19.001 --> 15:23.923
MARINE ZONE THREE

15:30.220 --> 15:34.058
Let's see here. Watershed nine, room four.

15:35.142 --> 15:36.143
Here it is.

15:39.521 --> 15:42.024
I'll just ring this bell.

15:54.787 --> 15:58.082
<i>First, greet them with</i> "bokora, bokora."

16:15.307 --> 16:17.142
What should I do?

16:17.226 --> 16:19.812
I'm from Udon Bebebe.

16:19.895 --> 16:23.357
Udon. I brought your udon noodles.

16:23.440 --> 16:27.861
The udon you ordered. I--

16:27.945 --> 16:29.488
Sir, wait a moment!

16:29.571 --> 16:31.991
Let me go!

16:34.243 --> 16:36.537
Calm down.

16:37.746 --> 16:42.793
Sea creatures eat anything that moves.

16:42.876 --> 16:48.298
Don't worry.
It'll let go if you stay still.

16:50.884 --> 16:54.972
Let me translate. I'll help you.

17:01.520 --> 17:02.896
<i>That's right.</i>

17:02.980 --> 17:05.566
<i>Seals are part sea creature
and part land dweller.</i>

17:07.067 --> 17:09.445
<i>A bilingual animal saved me.</i>

17:12.740 --> 17:14.575
"Eat. Udon."

17:15.492 --> 17:17.202
Here you are.

17:30.382 --> 17:31.717
You haven't paid!

17:35.304 --> 17:36.764
These shells.

17:36.847 --> 17:39.391
Turn into money at exchange.

17:39.475 --> 17:40.476
Exchange?

17:40.559 --> 17:45.272
Shells. Money of the sea. Things of value.

17:45.355 --> 17:47.608
I think I learned that at school.

17:49.193 --> 17:51.195
Thank you so much.

17:51.904 --> 17:53.655
You were a huge help.

17:53.739 --> 17:58.577
I'm a spotted seal. My name's Sagwan.

17:59.119 --> 18:03.665
Neighbors look out for each other.

18:05.042 --> 18:06.543
You live in Beast Apartments?

18:09.588 --> 18:11.048
Is that so?

18:12.174 --> 18:15.761
I lived in the ocean until six months ago.

18:15.844 --> 18:19.389
Now I teach
marine language at a university

18:19.473 --> 18:21.934
and study the ways of the land.

18:23.519 --> 18:26.980
Land. Very nice place.

18:27.064 --> 18:28.482
I like it very mu--

18:30.275 --> 18:31.443
Are you all right?

18:31.527 --> 18:33.862
You need to pay attention when you walk.

18:33.946 --> 18:35.781
The land is full of danger.

18:35.864 --> 18:39.326
It's okay. The ocean is the same.

18:39.409 --> 18:42.621
I guess that's probably true.

18:42.704 --> 18:47.251
It will never change. Even if I die.

18:53.257 --> 18:54.383
The ocean.

18:54.466 --> 18:58.262
Big fish eat small fish.

18:58.345 --> 19:02.099
Big fish get eaten by bigger fish.

19:02.182 --> 19:04.685
Then when bigger fish die,

19:04.768 --> 19:09.273
they get eaten by small fish and plankton.

19:11.233 --> 19:15.237
Creatures of the sea eat and are eaten.

19:15.320 --> 19:17.656
Eat and are eaten.

19:17.739 --> 19:19.616
We are all connected.

19:20.159 --> 19:23.078
We have no word for "devour."

19:23.162 --> 19:26.123
We live together in peace.

19:27.332 --> 19:30.002
"Eat and are eaten."

19:30.085 --> 19:33.046
But still in peace?

19:36.175 --> 19:37.718
<i>I never knew.</i>

19:38.510 --> 19:40.762
<i>Is there really a world like that?</i>

19:40.846 --> 19:44.266
<i>Here I am pondering the intricacies
of my relationship with herbivores,</i>

19:44.349 --> 19:46.602
<i>grappling with my own instincts,</i>

19:47.644 --> 19:49.438
<i>while that world is right next to me.</i>

19:55.903 --> 20:00.616
My room is 501. Let's have tea.

20:01.283 --> 20:04.661
I want to hear about you, Legoshi.

20:04.745 --> 20:07.080
Me? Sure.

20:19.384 --> 20:20.510
Come in.

20:21.845 --> 20:23.347
Pardon me.

20:23.430 --> 20:25.432
What's wrong, Legoshi?

20:25.515 --> 20:27.267
What are you doing?

20:27.351 --> 20:28.185
Put that away--

20:28.268 --> 20:30.312
I mean, put some clothes on!

20:30.395 --> 20:32.981
You can't be naked on the land.

20:33.523 --> 20:34.775
Really?

20:35.275 --> 20:37.361
Then I'll put clothes on.

20:37.444 --> 20:39.655
Sorry if I offended you.

20:39.738 --> 20:41.573
Oh, don't be...

20:43.575 --> 20:47.496
<i>I have to keep an open mind.
I shouldn't be judgmental.</i>

20:47.579 --> 20:50.707
Clothes are uncomfortable for you,
aren't they, Sagwan?

20:50.791 --> 20:52.251
You can stay like that.

20:54.294 --> 21:00.133
You eat and are eaten,
but you still live in peace.

21:00.217 --> 21:01.885
I just can't understand.

21:02.844 --> 21:05.847
On land, everyone struggles with this.

21:05.931 --> 21:09.017
Carnivores and herbivores
avoid each other.

21:09.101 --> 21:13.730
Legoshi, did something bad happen?

21:15.399 --> 21:21.571
There were rumors that a wolf
with a record of devouring moved in.

21:21.655 --> 21:23.156
Is that you?

21:23.782 --> 21:25.325
Word got around, huh?

21:25.951 --> 21:30.455
In the ocean, I'm a carnivore as well.
The same as you.

21:31.873 --> 21:35.210
In the ocean, we live with our sins.

21:36.044 --> 21:38.714
Isn't that difficult?

21:39.381 --> 21:40.799
Not at all.

21:41.842 --> 21:46.763
Looking at this makes me
feel like I'm floating in the sea.

21:46.847 --> 21:50.642
We are all connected,
so everything is balanced.

21:55.105 --> 22:01.445
<i>Being around him makes me feel like
I'm speaking with the ocean itself.</i>

22:02.279 --> 22:04.948
<i>I get this sense of weightlessness.</i>

22:06.491 --> 22:07.576
<i>You know,</i>

22:08.744 --> 22:09.995
<i>I think I like this guy.</i>

23:36.915 --> 23:41.920
Subtitle translation by: Thomas Grathwol
